{"repositoryId":1355136925,"availability":"available","full":"Tomt2816/typephp","name":"typephp","description":"Compile PHP source code into native machine code ahead of time, producing executables, extensions, and shared libraries with familiar PHP syntax.","category":"Developer tools","language":null,"stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-02T19:08:49Z","updated":"2026-10-12T18:58:51Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tomt2816.github.io","topics":["application-framework","c","cli","cpp","daemon","docker","linux","native","offline-first","php","privacy","sensevoice","speech-recognition","typephp","voice-input","webman","windows","workerman","zig"],"demo":"https://tomt2816.github.io/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.565Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.565Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.565Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.565Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["typephp is a free tool that takes your PHP code and turns it into a standalone executable file for Windows. Instead of needing a web server or PHP installed, you get a single .exe file that runs like any normal program. This makes sharing your PHP projects with friends, clients, or colleagues incredibly simple—they just double-click and run.","If you have ever written PHP scripts or used tools like WordPress, you know the usual hassle of setting up a server. typephp removes all that friction. You write your PHP code as usual, then typephp compiles it into a native Windows application. No extra software needed on the target machine."],"features":["You built a small business inventory tool in PHP for your own use. Now your accountant wants to use it too, but they don't have PHP installed. With typephp, you give them one file and it just works.","You are a freelancer delivering a custom PHP solution. Instead of sending a messy folder with installation instructions, you send a single polished .exe file. Your client double-clicks and it runs. Professional and…","You want to protect your source code. When you compile PHP to a native binary, your original code is not directly readable. This offers a layer of protection if you distribute your app publicly. (Note: no method is 100%…","You just hate the command line. You want your PHP program to behave like a regular Windows application—click an icon, a window opens, done. That's exactly what typephp delivers."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Tomt2816/typephp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a4f9442e61c6ef9c20c047dc4535eaefde42403586e5d7876dc2ff8d7983a815","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.695Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.695Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"typephp is a free tool that takes your PHP code and turns it into a standalone executable file for Windows. Instead of needing a web server or PHP installed, you get a single .exe file that runs like any normal program. This makes sharing your PHP projects with friends, clients, or colleagues incredibly simple—they just double-click and run.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Tomt2816/typephp/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a4f9442e61c6ef9c20c047dc4535eaefde42403586e5d7876dc2ff8d7983a815","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Tomt2816/typephp/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.696Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-12T18:58:51Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Tomt2816/typephp/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.696Z","hash":"a4f9442e61c6ef9c20c047dc4535eaefde42403586e5d7876dc2ff8d7983a815","originalBytes":10721,"storedBytes":10721,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["php","typephp","file","folder","command","exe","windows","compiled","compile","run","app","just","code","files","need","same","see","what","any","download","one","prompt","step","type","want","hello.exe","hello.php","now","press","error","g